{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NAVZiGRjy8aoXJ3aMuxjfG","type":"tool_result","content":"**Title:** Mind the Gap: a Spectral Analysis of Rank Collapse and Signal Propagation in Attention Layers\n\n**Authors:** Thiziri Nait Saada, Alireza Naderi, Jared Tanner\n\n**Venue:** The arXiv listing's comments field names the International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML) as the venue. No proceedings volume or page numbers are given. The arXiv identifier is 2410.07799, and this is version 3, revised June 16, 2025.\n\n**Rank collapse in the abstract:** The abstract separates three forms:\n\n- **Rank collapse in depth:** tokens converge to a single representation as they pass through layers. It arises from repeated matrix multiplications.\n- **Rank collapse in width:** \"rank collapse in width, which occurs as the context length increases.\" The authors present this as a challenge unique to softmax attention layers.\n- The authors attribute the width form to a spectral gap between the two largest singular values of the attention matrix. They say this gap worsens the depth collapse and the gradient problems. Their proposed fix is removing the outlier eigenvalue(s)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f42d925-3fb0-401c-b4de-561355f745c0","uuid":"560c3170-7e31-4ed5-9f19-59050180a072","timestamp":"2026-10-31T07:25:44.085Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":44850,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Title:** Mind the Gap: a Spectral Analysis of Rank Collapse and Signal Propagation in Attention Layers\n\n**Authors:** Thiziri Nait Saada, Alireza Naderi, Jared Tanner\n\n**Venue:** The arXiv listing's comments field names the International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML) as the venue. No proceedings volume or page numbers are given. The arXiv identifier is 2410.07799, and this is version 3, revised June 16, 2025.\n\n**Rank collapse in the abstract:** The abstract separates three forms:\n\n- **Rank collapse in depth:** tokens converge to a single representation as they pass through layers. It arises from repeated matrix multiplications.\n- **Rank collapse in width:** \"rank collapse in width, which occurs as the context length increases.\" The authors present this as a challenge unique to softmax attention layers.\n- The authors attribute the width form to a spectral gap between the two largest singular values of the attention matrix. They say this gap worsens the depth collapse and the gradient problems. Their proposed fix is removing the outlier eigenvalue(s).","durationMs":4054,"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.07799"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NAVZiGRjy8aoXJ3aMuxjfG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
