{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kbvi5Ltsjox1LAxozSpGd4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Kolchinsky Tracey \"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances\" Entropy 2017 19(7) 361\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.02419\"},{\"title\":\"Entropy (Jul 2017)\",\"url\":\"https://doaj.org/article/3ff7dff6b2c8436191ba69a82c555693\"},{\"title\":\"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances\",\"url\":\"https://ar5iv.arxiv.org/html/1706.02419\"},{\"title\":\"export.arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://export.arxiv.org/pdf/1706.02419\"},{\"title\":\"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances\",\"url\":\"https://deepai.org/publication/estimating-mixture-entropy-with-pairwise-distances\"},{\"title\":\"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances\",\"url\":\"https://api.deepai.org/publication/estimating-mixture-entropy-with-pairwise-distances\"},{\"title\":\"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances\",\"url\":\"https://cdnjs.deepai.org/publication/estimating-mixture-entropy-with-pairwise-distances\"},{\"title\":\"Current browse context:\",\"url\":\"https://export.arxiv.org/abs/1706.02419?context=cs\"},{\"title\":\"Next Article in Journal\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/1099-4300/19/7/361/xml\"},{\"title\":\"Computer Science > Information Theory\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.com/abs/1706.02419\"}]\n\nThe paper is on arXiv and the Entropy journal. Kolchinsky and Tracey propose a family of mixture-entropy estimators built from a pairwise distance between mixture components. Entropy (Jul 2017) lists the authors as Artemy Kolchinsky and Brendan D. Tracey, DOI 10.3390/e19070361, Vol. 19, no. 7, p. 361.\n\n- **Motivation:** It is often necessary to compute the entropy of a mixture, but, in most cases, this quantity has no closed-form expression, making some form of approximation necessary.\n- **Bounds:** The authors prove this family includes lower and upper bounds on the mixture entropy. The Chernoff α-divergence gives a lower bound when chosen as the distance function, with the Bhattacharyya distance providing the tightest lower bound for components that are symmetric and members of a location family. The Kullback–Leibler divergence gives an upper bound when used as the distance function.\n- **Exactness:** The family can compute the exact mixture entropy when the component distributions are grouped into well-separated clusters, a property not shared by other analytic estimators of entropy.\n- **Applications:** Closed-form expressions of these bounds are given for mixtures of Gaussians, with discussion of applications to mutual information estimation.\n\n**Caveat on the published version:** The arXiv version (v4) includes an author's note stating that the published version of this manuscript (Kolchinsky and Tracey, Entropy 2017, 19(7), 361; doi:10.3390/e19070361) contains a mistake. The arXiv v4 text also has garbled excerpts on which distance gives which bound, so check the bound assignments against the paper itself before relying on them.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f42d925-3fb0-401c-b4de-561355f745c0","uuid":"a3c19181-f784-43bf-81f0-f38a7f831425","timestamp":"2026-10-31T07:25:49.184Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Kolchinsky Tracey \"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances\" Entropy 2017 19(7) 361","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01LC216Q5Q4x319Ra5okrmzT","content":[{"title":"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.02419"},{"title":"Entropy (Jul 2017)","url":"https://doaj.org/article/3ff7dff6b2c8436191ba69a82c555693"},{"title":"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances","url":"https://ar5iv.arxiv.org/html/1706.02419"},{"title":"export.arxiv.org","url":"https://export.arxiv.org/pdf/1706.02419"},{"title":"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances","url":"https://deepai.org/publication/estimating-mixture-entropy-with-pairwise-distances"},{"title":"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances","url":"https://api.deepai.org/publication/estimating-mixture-entropy-with-pairwise-distances"},{"title":"Estimating Mixture Entropy with Pairwise Distances","url":"https://cdnjs.deepai.org/publication/estimating-mixture-entropy-with-pairwise-distances"},{"title":"Current browse context:","url":"https://export.arxiv.org/abs/1706.02419?context=cs"},{"title":"Next Article in Journal","url":"https://www.mdpi.com/1099-4300/19/7/361/xml"},{"title":"Computer Science > Information Theory","url":"https://arxiv.com/abs/1706.02419"}]},"The paper is on arXiv and the Entropy journal. Kolchinsky and Tracey propose a family of mixture-entropy estimators built from a pairwise distance between mixture components. Entropy (Jul 2017) lists the authors as Artemy Kolchinsky and Brendan D. Tracey, DOI 10.3390/e19070361, Vol. 19, no. 7, p. 361.\n\n- **Motivation:** It is often necessary to compute the entropy of a mixture, but, in most cases, this quantity has no closed-form expression, making some form of approximation necessary.\n- **Bounds:** The authors prove this family includes lower and upper bounds on the mixture entropy. The Chernoff α-divergence gives a lower bound when chosen as the distance function, with the Bhattacharyya distance providing the tightest lower bound for components that are symmetric and members of a location family. The Kullback–Leibler divergence gives an upper bound when used as the distance function.\n- **Exactness:** The family can compute the exact mixture entropy when the component distributions are grouped into well-separated clusters, a property not shared by other analytic estimators of entropy.\n- **Applications:** Closed-form expressions of these bounds are given for mixtures of Gaussians, with discussion of applications to mutual information estimation.\n\n**Caveat on the published version:** The arXiv version (v4) includes an author's note stating that the published version of this manuscript (Kolchinsky and Tracey, Entropy 2017, 19(7), 361; doi:10.3390/e19070361) contains a mistake. The arXiv v4 text also has garbled excerpts on which distance gives which bound, so check the bound assignments against the paper itself before relying on them."],"durationSeconds":6.002686870000005,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Kbvi5Ltsjox1LAxozSpGd4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
