{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013mtfshWnchLAmhh65DNTCH","type":"tool_result","content":"The comment is: \"Corrects several errata in published version, in particular in Section V (bounds on mutual information).\" This means the arXiv version fixes several errors from the 2017 *Entropy* publication, mainly in the mutual information bounds in Section V.\n\nThe Chernoff α-divergence gives a lower bound on mixture entropy, with the Bhattacharyya distance giving the tightest lower bound for symmetric components in a location family. The Kullback-Leibler divergence gives an upper bound."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f42d925-3fb0-401c-b4de-561355f745c0","uuid":"7ed4e57b-0808-4a91-9219-6e181b4c76f9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T07:26:05.076Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":45162,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The comment is: \"Corrects several errata in published version, in particular in Section V (bounds on mutual information).\" This means the arXiv version fixes several errors from the 2017 *Entropy* publication, mainly in the mutual information bounds in Section V.\n\nThe Chernoff α-divergence gives a lower bound on mixture entropy, with the Bhattacharyya distance giving the tightest lower bound for symmetric components in a location family. The Kullback-Leibler divergence gives an upper bound.","durationMs":2504,"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.02419"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013mtfshWnchLAmhh65DNTCH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
