{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZvUwwN86jFnBWT61SKb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The paper is finished and compiles with no errors and no undefined citations or references: 12 pages, with a 218-word abstract. I titled it \"Initialization Sets the Direction of Attention Rank Change During Training\". I went through the language, formatting and structure checklists and looked over a low-resolution sheet of all the pages, which showed no layout problems.\n\n**Departures from the brief**\n- `paper_examples/` holds only a README, so style comes from the guide and `style_examples.md`.\n- The preamble adds one line defining `\\@trackname`, because `[final]` alone breaks `\\maketitle`. It also loads `amsthm`, `enumitem` and the algorithm packages.\n- The introduction has no method figure, because a table of claims and verdicts seemed more useful. Figures are the existing PNGs.\n- The outline is in `paper/OUTLINE.md`, the path the skill gives.\n\n**Where the paper differs from `REPORT.md`**\n\nI recomputed the numbers from `results/` and read the estimator code, and `REPORT.md` itself is unchanged. These differences are worth checking if you reuse the report:\n\n| Topic | `REPORT.md` | Paper |\n|---|---|---|\n| **MI scope (largest change)** | Doesn't say what the Î_BD numbers cover | They are joint over all 8 heads of a layer. Per head they are about 8× smaller at ε ≥ 1. |\n| **MI violations at ε=2** | 93% order task, 73% AG News | Those are layer-level; per head they are 35% and 15%. The paper gives both. |\n| **Seed spread** | \"I ≥ 1.04 nats\" | That is a mean; seeds range from 0.21 to 1.83, which the paper states. |\n| **Late U-shape** | Only under ×3 init or without signal | BERT also shows it, in 67% of cells. |\n| **Rank fall** | Only from peaked starts | Shuffled-label runs also dip: the last layer of `ag_L6_shuffled` drops 37%, then recovers. |\n| **\"Attractor band\"** | Both AG arms end near .06–.14 of n | Dropped. Layer 1 in the ×3 arm stays at about .32; only last layers converge (.06 and .09). |\n| **Low-entropy pruning, `ag_L6`** | Not mentioned | Significantly worse than random, by 1.4 pp (Wilcoxon p = .016). |\n| **Rise-time ratio, `ag_L6`** | 2.1 | That mean hides heavy tails; the median is 0.78. |\n| **Pruning p-values** | Mixed tests, unlabelled | Now labelled: two of the three CIFAR values are t-tests. |\n| **SST-2 accuracy** | 81.1 | 81.0 (mean 81.05). |\n\n**Citations**\n- \"Mind the Gap\" is by Nait Saada, Naderi and Tanner (ICML 2025), not \"Naderi et al.\".\n- Linformer's spectra come from pretrained RoBERTa models.\n- Michel et al. rank heads by mask sensitivity, and their 60% figure applies to BERT on SST-2.\n- The Kolchinsky & Tracey entry now points to the corrected arXiv version, because the journal version has errata in its mutual-information section.\n- I checked the core references online, except Hartigan & Hartigan, whose entry is unchanged and unchecked. The added dataset and ViT citations (`zhang2015character`, `krizhevsky2009learning`, `dosovitskiy2021image`) are from memory, so check those three before submission.\n\n**Remaining weaknesses**\n- The H4 refutation rests on Proposition 1 and the AG News trend in n. The order-task trend is noisy, and the per-head excess is small enough that a constant around 24 would fit any single n; only its growth with n counts against the claim.\n- Everything else in the report's Limitations section is carried into the paper.\n\nEverything is in `paper_draft/`; open `main.pdf`. I also added this run's lessons to the paper-writer memory."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":583,"cache_read_input_tokens":157208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":583},"output_tokens":785,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f42d925-3fb0-401c-b4de-561355f745c0","uuid":"828e5e91-ec6e-4fec-ad43-919cafeb8fe7","timestamp":"2026-10-31T07:30:26.742Z","request_id":"req_011CgZvUwfW4MYMnDDrPef84"}
